    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **255 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the two new `AcceptanceTest` cases for locality.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field derived from an owner's city using the fixed city-to-region table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema. This regenerates the `OwnerDto` at build time so the field is serialized in `GET /api/owners/{id}` responses.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `locality` backed by a new `locality(Owner)` default method that maps the city via the pinned table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`), returning `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any other/unlisted city.\n\nThis fits the existing pattern: `locality` is a derived, read-only field computed on read alongside `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`, and `membershipTier` \u2014 no new endpoint, storage, or write path needed, matching the project's OfficeFloor `RespondWithOwner \u2192 OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` flow.",
